# DTF tier manifest: generic-conditional-put (artifact-keeper#4186)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single.
#
# THE FEATURE (artifact-keeper#4186, backend PR #4983)
# `PUT /api/v1/repositories/{key}/artifacts/{path}` honours If-Match /
# If-None-Match against the artifact's ETag (its quoted SHA-256, now on the
# 201 and the download). Racing conditional PUTs on one ETag (or
# If-None-Match: * on a free path) have exactly one 201; the others get 412
# PRECONDITION_FAILED. A stale If-Match is 412 and changes nothing. On a
# versioning-enabled repository the racers append exactly one revision. A
# malformed precondition is 400.
#
# Split out of generic-concurrent-put-contract (artifact-keeper-test#648),
# which gates the #4832 fix on 1.11.x: these cases are a 1.12.0 FEATURE and
# are red on every 1.11.x image, so they live in their own tier and a
# features-1.12.0 gate group.
#
# RED image: ak-backend:1.11.5 (headers ignored: If-Match racers all 409,
# If-None-Match racers 1x201 + 409s, versioned racers all 201, no ETag,
# malformed header 409). GREEN: 1.12.0 with #4186 (main from 368561ea).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: 16 concurrent uploads (x3 waves) plus ~20 calls back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
